{
  "reports": [
    {
      "title": "Incorrect Instantaneous Overcurrent Setting Causes Feeder 7 Lockout During Cold Load Restoration",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "Feeder 7 relay setting group S3 had an instantaneous pickup of 1,200 A, intended for normal load.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The cold-load pickup current for the feeder was calculated to reach 1,950 A rms for twelve cycles.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "An operator did not change the setting group to S4, which contained the 2,000 A cold-load instantaneous setting.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The triac gate was verified open, eliminating the capacitor bank's MT1-to-MT2 conduction as a cause.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "At 09:12:33.54, breaker 52-1 closed to restore power to Synthetic Feeder 7.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Feeder 7 supplied 87 induction motors and one triac-switched capacitor bank at a pre-outage load of 41 MW.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "SCADA indicated phase A current saturated at 1,200 A during the first 100 ms after closing.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [4]
        },
        {
          "text": "The independent phase A CT channel measured a peak current of 2,130 A rms for nine cycles.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [4, 5]
        },
        {
          "text": "The relay's 50 instantaneous element tripped at 09:12:33.72 when the measured current exceeded the 1,200 A setting.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 7]
        },
        {
          "text": "Breaker 52-1 opened at 09:12:33.80, interrupting the feeder current with a 32 ms opening time.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "Reclosing relay automatically reclosed breaker 52-1 after a 15 second dead time at 09:12:48.72.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The second reclose caused another 50 trip, and the 86 lockout relay sealed the breaker open.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [10]
        },
        {
          "text": "Synthetic Feeder 7 remained de-energized for 43 minutes until an operator remotely switched the setting group.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9, 11]
        },
        {
          "text": "The 29.4 MWh energy loss was calculated as 41 MW times the 43 minute outage duration.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "Three industrial chillers tripped on undervoltage because their motors decelerated during the 15 second dead time.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The false lockout caused a ten minute overrun beyond the corridor's allowed 30 minute restoration standard.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "An engineer changed relay setting group to S4 at 09:55, raising instantaneous pickup to 2,000 A.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The operator manually closed breaker 52-1 at 09:56, and the feeder successfully picked up cold load.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [16]
        },
        {
          "text": "A new pre-restoration checklist now requires confirmation that the relay active setting group matches the outage context.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The triac controller's firmware was updated to prevent false gate signals during future breaker operations.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        }
      ],
      "distractor_seeds": [
        "The annual maintenance schedule for the substation's relays had been completed exactly six months before the restoration date.",
        "Feeder 7's parallel path through the normally-open tie switch was unavailable due to a scheduled repair on the neighboring feeder.",
        "The calibration curve for the CT used in the protection relay was certified within the accuracy class 5P20, as per factory documentation.",
        "The SCADA alarm server experienced a time skew of 300 milliseconds but that did not affect the event reconstruction.",
        "The operator attended a human factors training session on cold-load pickup restoration earlier in the year.",
        "A lightning spike hit the substation's station service transformer, but its surge arrester operated and the event did not spread.",
        "The triac module's MT1 terminal was wired with a 10-ohm gate resistor, while the gate was tied to the neutral reference.",
        "Load management software predicted that motor load on feeder 7 would rise by 2% after each restoration attempt.",
        "The breakers at the substation were AC-emergency powered for two minutes before the restoration, but the supply was restored.",
        "An engineer had proposed to use setting group S4 also for the summer peaking season, but the proposal was deferred.",
        "The substation's battery voltage was 128.5 V, which is within the control circuit operating range.",
        "The outage management system displayed feeder 7 as pending a manual inspection because of a separate low-voltage complaint."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Ground Fault Relay Miscoordination Lockout on Synthetic Feeder 12 After Recloser Setting Mismatch",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "Substation relay 51N on feeder 12 had a time-overcurrent pickup of 1,200 A with a 0.6 s time dial.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Recloser R-2's time dial was erroneously set to 2.0 after the controller replacement.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The coordination study for feeder 12 required recloser R-2 to trip in 0.3 s for ground faults above 1,500 A.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The triac gate was held off by the controller, so the capacitor bank switch was not closed.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "At 10:27:15, breaker 52-2 at Synthetic Substation B closed to energize Synthetic Feeder 12.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A tree squirrel touched phase B terminal on a downstream transformer, initiating a solid ground fault.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [4]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fault current measured by the feeder neutral CT reached 1,800 A rms at 10:27:18.35.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [5]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fault persisted for 0.8 seconds as recloser R-2 did not assert its trip output.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [5]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 10:27:19.01, the 51N ground relay tripped breaker 52-2 after a 0.65 s delay.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 6, 7]
        },
        {
          "text": "Breaker 52-2 opened in 3 cycles, isolating the entire feeder from the source.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "ANSI 86 lockout relay energized on the feeder ground fault trip, sealing the breaker open.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "Recloser R-2's own ground fault unit would have operated at 1.4 seconds, after the substation breaker had already cleared.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [1, 8]
        },
        {
          "text": "Synthetic Feeder 12 remained de-energized for one hour twenty minutes, causing a load loss of 13.5 MW.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9, 10]
        },
        {
          "text": "The unsupplied energy was 18 MWh, equal to 13.5 MW times 80 minutes.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "Two industrial plants shut down due to the feeder outage, but their restart took 2 hours.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The feeder's 23 kV nominal voltage disappeared, so all downstream controllers declared a loss-of-voltage event.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 11:45, an engineer remotely changed recloser R-2's setting group to group 2, restoring a 0.5 s time dial.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Operators closed breaker 52-2 at 11:47, after confirming the feeder was in a normal no-fault condition.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [16]
        },
        {
          "text": "A new verification step requires every recloser controller setting change to be cross-checked against the feeder's coordination study.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The triac-based remote switching module was inspected, and its MT1-MT2 isolation was confirmed for future restoration.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        }
      ],
      "distractor_seeds": [
        "A lightning strike had caused the original feeder fault four hours earlier, but the feeder had been repaired and tested.",
        "Feeder 12's underground cable section had a known sheath voltage limiting device that was not affected by the ground fault.",
        "The substation's battery charger produced 54.2 V without ripple, and alarms were silent before the restoration.",
        "Recloser R-2's controller was replaced with an identical model, but its old settings were stored in a backup file.",
        "The utility's communication system reported phase loss on a microwave link during the event, but that link was not critical.",
        "The squirrel was later classified as a gray squirrel weighing 0.5 kg, based on evidence at the transformer bushing.",
        "An adjacent feeder carried a 6 MW block of load for the same industrial park, which might have allowed load transfer.",
        "The neutral CT installation on feeder 12 had been checked for polarity one year before, and it was correct.",
        "A training module on recloser setting verification was available but had not been downloaded by the field crew.",
        "The station battery voltage was recorded at 129.2 V at the moment of the close command, which is within regulation.",
        "The setting group 2 of recloser R-2 contains the correct 0.5 time dial for the synthetic feeder's coordination study.",
        "The weather was dry and sunny with a temperature of 18°C, which did not affect insulation resistance."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
